From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Fix uninitialized variable in the RTree midphase

The two argument processResults() passes an uninitialized float as the
newMaxT in/out parameter of the three argument one, which reads it before
writing it, both to shrink the ray distance and to clamp what a hit
callback returns. Whether that garbage is smaller than a real hit
distance decides whether the raycast keeps looking, so the results depend
on the stack contents.

This is the RTree half of the PhysX 4.1 patch "Fix Uninitialized
Variables", forward ported to 5.9.0. Its other half, the uninitialized
bool array in GuPCMTriangleContactGen.cpp, has been fixed upstream.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/geomutils/src/mesh/GuMidphaseRTree.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/geomutils/src/mesh/GuMidphaseRTree.cpp b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/geomutils/src/mesh/GuMidphaseRTree.cpp
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/geomutils/src/mesh/GuMidphaseRTree.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/geomutils/src/mesh/GuMidphaseRTree.cpp
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ struct RayRTreeCallback : RTree::CallbackRaycast, RTree::Callback
 
 	virtual bool processResults(PxU32 numTouched, PxU32* touched) PX_OVERRIDE
 	{
-		PxF32 dummy;
+		PxF32 dummy = 0;
 		return RayRTreeCallback::processResults(numTouched, touched, dummy);
 	}
 
